    {
      "type": "table",
      "id": "table-00001",
      "summary": "An illustration (table) shows the structures of monomers the polymers made and their uses. Adipic acid reacts with Hexamethylenediamine to yield Nylon 66 used in Fibers clothing tire cord. The structure of adipic acid shows a green hydroxyl group bonded to a carbonyl group that is bonded to 4 methylene groups and then a carbonyl group bonded to green hydroxyl group. Hexamethylenediamine shows a blue amino group bonded to a chain of 6 methylene groups and then a blue amino group. Dimethyl terephthalate reacts with Ethylene glycol to yield Dacron Mylar and Terylene used in Fibers clothing films tire cord. The structure of Dimethyl terephthalate shows a benzene bonded to a carbonyl group at C1 and C4. Each carbonyl group is bonded to a green methoxide group. Ethylene glycol shows a blue hydroxyl group bonded to a chain of two methylene groups and then a blue hydroxyl group. Caprolactam yields Nylon 6 and Perlon used in Fibers castings. Caprolactam shows a cycloheptane ring with a blue nitrogen monohydride; the ring is double bonded to a pink oxygen. Diphenyl carbonate reacts with Bisphenol A to yield Lexan and polycarbonate used in Equipment housing molded articles. Diphenyl carbonate shows a carbonyl group bonded to two green oxygen atoms on both sides. Each green oxygen is bonded to a benzene ring. Bisphenol A shows a carbon bonded to two methyl groups and two phenols in which the hydroxyl groups are blue. Toluene-2 6-diisocyanate reacts with Poly(2-butene-1 4-diol) to yield Polyurethane and Spandex used in Fibers coatings foams. Toluene-2 6-diisocyanate shows a carbonyl group double bonded to a nitrogen bonded to a benzene that is bonded to a methyl group and a nitrogen that is double bonded to a carbonyl group. Poly(2-butene-1 4-diol) shows a blue hydroxyl group bonded to a methylene group bonded to a methine group double bonded to a methine group bonded to a methylene group bonded to a blue hydroxyl group. The structure except the hydroxyl groups is shown inside parentheses with subscript n.",
      "title": {
        "segmentId": "m00247:table-title:table-00001-title",
        "text": "Some Common Step-Growth Polymers and Their Uses"
      },
